// §2.2: "Verilog-AMS HDL source text files shall be a stream of lexical
// tokens", and the list that follows names `comment` as one of the seven token
// types — so a comment SEPARATES the two tokens around it.
//
// The regression this pins: the preprocessor used to re-emit only the NEWLINES
// a block comment contained, which is enough for a multi-line comment and
// welds a single-line one. `1/*c*/2` reached the lexer as the single integer
// literal 12 and compiled silently into the device. `</*c*/=` welded into the
// operator `<=` the same way.
//
// Correct behaviour is a syntax error here: `1` and `2` are two adjacent
// primaries, which no A.8.3 production derives.
module ch2_comment_separator(p, n);
  inout p, n;
  electrical p, n;
  analog I(p, n) <+ (1/*c*/2) * V(p, n);
endmodule
